    "created_at": "2024-03-29T11:50:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-29T11:50:52Z",
    "body": "> It seems there is no way to both check if sudo has cached the password, and avoid sudo sending spamming logs : ( For security reasons, I don't think upstream will add the feature like that.\r\n\r\nI do not understand why upstream would not add such a feature. So I don't understand the security implication of silently being able to check caching.\r\n\r\nIn any case, others have considered this exact issue and written code to determine caching without log spamming: https://unix.stackexchange.com/a/332143. So a possible solution would be to reimplement this solution in starship.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
